#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION Classification and provenance"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Every table and column is classified by sensitivity and tagged with provenance from the moment it lands."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: governance · depends on: [CAP-CATALOG]{1}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Label every table by sensitivity and provenance from the moment it lands."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Tags added at gold come too late to protect bronze. Provenance tags make drops provable ([P12]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Governed `classification` (T0–T4) and `provenance` (real, simulated, derived) tags."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "A default policy for unclassified data; a separate catalog for T4."
msgstr ""

