#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Every table carries a classification (T0 public aggregate, T1 internal, T2 de-identified, T3 identifiable, T4 special category) and a provenance (real, simulated, derived)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "The daily fitness function finds no untagged table."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Data not yet classified is blocked by default until classification has run.{1}*Example:* A table loaded from a partner arrives unclassified; analysts cannot read it until classification has run and a steward has confirmed it as T3."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "A new unclassified table is unreadable by analysts."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "T4 data lives in its own catalog and storage, and each grant on it is approved by its steward."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "T4 tables exist only in the T4 catalog; its grants trace to approvals."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Tags are applied where data enters (landing and bronze), not added at gold."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Bronze tables carry the tags."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Simulated data lives only in sandbox catalogs, and derived data is built only from tagged tables."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "No table tagged simulated is outside a sandbox catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Attributes follow a default classification by kind: data that identifies or locates a person is at least T3; special-category data under the applicable data-protection law, and child-protection and wellbeing records, are T4. Exceptions are recorded with a reason.{1}*Example:* A column of birth dates is T3 by default and a column of health conditions T4; classifying the birth dates lower requires a recorded reason."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "A check compares column classifications with the default table and lists exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "CAP-CLASSIFICATION.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "Every personal-data element declares its purpose and legal basis in the catalog; an element with no consuming process or measure at its periodic review is proposed for removal.{1}*Example:* The element 'guardian occupation' has had no consuming report or process for a year, so its review proposes removing it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-classification.md
msgid "A report lists personal-data elements without a purpose or without a consumer."
msgstr ""

